<title>BRAZIL: Brazil to have coffee crop forecast system by 1998.</title>
<headline>Brazil to have coffee crop forecast system by 1998.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's new coffee council does not expect to have a reliable crop forecasting system in place until 1998, said the head of the primary commodities department of the Industry and Commerce Ministry.</p>
<p>&quot;We are looking for alternatives, there have already been some technical meetings,&quot; Mauricio Assis told reporters after a meeting with private coffee sector representatives.</p>
<p>The drawing up of a reliable crop forecasting system is one of the goals of the new coffee council, called the CDPC, which unites the private and the public sector.</p>
<p>The meeting today of council members was to prepare for the next full session of the CDPC to be held on May 5 in Belo Horizonte.</p>
<p>((-Joelle Diderich, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 248 5414))</p>
